# Import fixtures stand in for provider output, so their bytes are the test input rather than
# source code. Checking them out with native line endings breaks the tests that construct CRLF
# input themselves: `importOfficialApp.test.ts` does `.replace(/\n/g, '\r\n')`, which turns an
# already-CRLF fixture into `\r\r\n` and inflates every reported line number.
*.txt -text
